<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n29637" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">montŭōsus</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">montōsus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj.
		mons, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>mountainous, full of mountains</i> (class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">regio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Planc. 9, 22</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cum locis ipsis delectemur, montuosis etiam,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Lael. 19, 68</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">loci,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Part. 10, 36</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">frutex,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					12, 13, 28, § 48</span></i>
			.—Form montosa, <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 7,
				744</span></i>. —<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">montŭōsa</span></b> ,
				ōrum, n., <i>mountain regions, mountainous parts</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">montuosa Ciliciae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					11, 53, 116, § 280</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Vulg. Jer. 17, 26</span></i>.</div>
